# GD-17 (round 19, writer 10): w now states `fulfils a`, so it is a settlement (E §5 step 2: "A movement whose fulfils
# names an adjustment (a settlement) isn't measured"), as snap14 took any move binding over adjustments to be; without
# it w is measured and reads the adjustments it makes (E5_binding_over_adjustments_measured). The old comment:
# Fault shape w_on (writer 7's brief, item 3): w_on is a date input whose one row (governs always) is in a version known
# 2026-09-01; move w binds a in adjustments on w_on. At cuts before that version w_on has no row, a hole whose possible
# days are any day. L §5.7: "a binding whose day is a hole binds nothing where no thing could be alive on its possible
# days"; L §5.14.3: no adjustment exists before the version that makes it (raise_2026, known 2026-05-01). As known
# 2026-04-30 no adjustment exists: the binding binds nothing, count 0 (q6). As known 2026-06-30 the adjustment of
# wage[2026-03] exists and could fall on w_on: the binding is a hole (q5), and so is what reads it. (Writer 6's
# REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §4.6 on this shape is gone: the no-law question is a hole.)
=== m.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source plan "plan"
source act "act"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind wages: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place savings: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_amt: money PLN
input wage_dom: int
input w_on: date
input keep: money PLN
input sweep_dom: int
def net[m in months]: money PLN = wage_amt at start_of(m)

move wage[m in months]: wages
  on day_of(m, wage_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount net[m]

move w[a in adjustments on w_on where a.adjusts in wages]: transfers
  on w_on
  leg cash from world to konto amount a.change
  fulfils a

move sweep[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, sweep_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to savings amount max(0 PLN, bal(konto, end_of(m) - 1 day) from day_of(m, sweep_dom) - keep)

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  wage_amt = 5 000.00 PLN "umowa"
  wage_dom = 10 "umowa"
  sweep_dom = 20 "own"
  keep = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
  opening[savings] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

version raise_2026
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-05-01
  replace wage_amt = 5 500.00 PLN "aneks"

version back_pay_day
  cite act
  governs always
  known 2026-09-01
  w_on = 2026-09-15 "aneks"

ask q5: count(a in adjustments on w_on) as known 2026-06-30
ask q6: count(a in adjustments on w_on) as known 2026-04-30
=== expect
q5: ? ...
  cut 2026-06-30
q6: 0
  cut 2026-04-30
...
